{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22114 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "Oxytroflavoside B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to JM1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Oxytroflavoside B directly targets VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one and Glycitein. Both of these compounds are known to have targets that ultimately converge on JM1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Oxytroflavoside B may influence JM1 through the activation of VMRC-LCP, which is a common target across several compounds. This suggests that Oxytroflavoside B could exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of VMRC-LCP, which in turn affects JM1. The evidence supports a central role for VMRC-LCP in this relationship, with Oxytroflavoside B acting as a potential activator or modulator of this critical node in the pathway.",
